'@@author Atharva005
@startuml
title Display help for a known topic
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EDF3F8
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #526477
skinparam ArrowColor #526477
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox

actor "User" as User
participant "ui:Ui" as UI
participant "ConsoleHelper" as Console
participant "parser:Parser" as Parser

Console -> UI : readLine()
User -> UI : help view
UI --> Console : input

Console -> Parser : parse("help view")
create participant "help:HelpCommand" as Help
Parser -> Help : HelpCommand("view")
note right of Help
  Normalize the topic with Locale.ROOT
  and look up TOPIC_HELP.
end note
Help --> Parser : initialized helpCommand
Parser --> Console : helpCommand
Console -> Help : execute(activities, storage)
Help --> Console : CommandResult(message, false)
Console -> UI : showMessage(result.getMessage())
UI --> User : result message

note over Console, UI
  This sequence assumes one known topic.
  Bare help instead constructs HelpCommand() for OVERVIEW.
  Extra topic words are rejected before construction.
  An unknown topic causes the constructor to throw ParseException.
  Help and rejected input never request saving or exit.
  Non-ASCII command words are rejected before dispatch.
  Add/edit help includes printable-ASCII names and duplicate/clash rules.
end note
@enduml
'@@author
